Cuboidz <Dieter.Bercx@gmail.com> writes:

> 1) How thoroughly do you search each dungeon level before continuing
> to the next? Do you try to discover all secret rooms (including shops

Generally I walk through every corridor to the end, I want each level
completely mapped out so I don't miss any useful item that may be there.
And I walk around each room by the walls to find vault entrances.
When I don't yet have a pick-axe at the early game, I search and open the
doors to the vault teleporters, and search until the teleporter gets
marked, so I can spot it when I come back with a pick-axe.

> and vaults)? Also, how many times do you search one spot before
> deciding nothing's there (using "n[number]s")?

I don't start every search by moving Southeast. When I suspect there might
be a hidden door in a room, I start in a corner, use 9s, then move three
steps in one direction, use 9s there, move another three steps and so on.
Every search turn searches all the adjacent wall squares, so I use this
invormation to get 9 searches for each wall square without actually using
the s command on every square.

> 2) Is "leveling" a good idea in nethack, e.g. running around until you
> see a monster to kill (to gain experience)?

Generally not. When you have explored the whole level, staying there just
to wait more monsters to get created only consumes food. You can as well
descend to the next level and kill the monsters there while exploring the
level. That way you can probably get yourself properly equipped earlier.

> 3) Do you make the effort of picking up every single item, even if you
> don't need it, in order to sell it in a shop - unless the load would

Sometimes I may carry stuff to a shop that buys it, if there is a suitable
shop on the same level, but not to shops on other dungeon levels.
I generally leave behind everything I know I don't need.

> burden you, or course? Even more, do you run back for items you left
> because you couldn't carry any more items (for the same purpose of
> selling them)?

Not for selling, but to get stuff I stashed for later use.

